Re `print_summary`: we can just simply not print anything if there are no samples to summarize from.

Re model with only deterministic: currently, we skip postprocessing if there are no latent variables in the model. The main reason is: for vectorized postprocess_fn, we need some values to vmap over. To fix the issue, we can replace [vmap(postprocess_fn)](https://github.com/pyro-ppl/numpyro/blob/c110053eb95f5398f11b93ce3efa21de4559012c/numpyro/infer/mcmc.py#L406) by a call `ensure_vmap(postprocess_fn)`, where `ensure_vmap` can take empty argument. Something like
```
def ensure_vmap(fn, batch_size=None):
    def wrapper(x):
        x_arrays = jax.tree.flatten(x)[0]
        if len(x_arrays) > 0:
            return vmap(fn)(x)
        else:
            assert batch_size is not None
            return jax.tree.map(lambda x: jnp.broadcast_to(x, (batch_size,) + jnp.shape(x)), fn(x))

    return wrapper
```
